{%- comment -%}
  ═══ LBASS — CAMPAIGN BADGE (2026-09-09) ═══

  Announces the running «‑30% على القطعة الثانية» offer. Renders nothing unless
  snippets/lbass-promo.liquid says this product is in the campaign.

  ── THE WORDING IS THE COMPLIANCE CONTROL, NOT DECORATION ────────────────────
  The reference design that prompted this work showed a red circle reading
  «‑33%» beside a struck-through price. That layout is correct ONLY when the
  item itself is marked down. Under this campaign it is not — the discount lands
  on the SECOND item in the basket. So the badge always carries its object:

      RENDERED   «‑30% على الثانية»
      RENDERED   «زيد قطعة ثانية وخد ‑30% عليها»
      NEVER      «‑30%» alone, in a circle or anywhere else
      NEVER      a struck-through price sourced from this campaign

  Drop the words «على الثانية» and the badge becomes a claim that this piece is
  30% off, which it is not, and the page stops matching checkout. If a future
  campaign really does mark items down, that belongs in `compare_at_price` and
  snippets/lbass-price.liquid renders it automatically — not here.

  ── PERCENTAGE SYNC (MANUAL — READ THIS) ─────────────────────────────────────
  Liquid cannot read an automatic discount, so `settings.promo_second_pct` is a
  copy of the rate configured in Shopify Admin → Discounts. THEY MUST MATCH.
  Change one, change the other in the same sitting. The number a shopper is
  actually charged always comes from Shopify; this setting only controls what
  the page claims. A mismatch is a false advertisement, not a cosmetic bug.

  ── PARAMETERS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    product   required
    format    'ribbon' (default) — corner ribbon for a card image
              NOT `variant` — that word means a product variant everywhere
              else in this theme, including snippets/lbass-price.liquid
              'line'             — one-line note for a card body
              'pdp'              — fuller explanation for the product page
    active    optional — 'yes' | 'no'. A verdict the caller ALREADY got from
              lbass-promo. Omit it and this file asks lbass-promo itself.

  ── WHY `active` EXISTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Shopify's performance guidance is to flatten nested renders, especially inside
  loops (shopify.dev → "Flatten nested render calls"). A collection page loops up
  to 250 cards, and each card shows TWO badges (ribbon + line). Self-checking
  both would run lbass-promo twice per card — 500 extra nested renders per page
  for a verdict that cannot change between them.

  So lbass-product-card asks ONCE and passes the answer down. lbass-promo stays
  the single source of truth: this file never re-implements the rule, it only
  accepts an answer that came from there.

  STRINGS, NOT BOOLEANS, on purpose. In Liquid `false == blank` is true, so a
  boolean `active: false` is indistinguishable from "argument not passed" and
  the fallback would fire on exactly the products meant to be excluded.

  CSS lives in snippets/lbass-promo-css.liquid, rendered once per document.

  USAGE
      {% render 'lbass-promo-badge', product: product, format: 'ribbon' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  if active == 'yes'
    assign lb_on = true
  elsif active == 'no'
    assign lb_on = false
  else
    assign lb_on = nil
  endif
-%}
{%- if lb_on == nil -%}
  {%- capture lb_promo_s %}{% render 'lbass-promo', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- assign lb_promo_s = lb_promo_s | strip -%}
  {%- assign lb_on = false -%}
  {%- if lb_promo_s == '1' -%}{%- assign lb_on = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if lb_on -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign lb_v = format | default: 'ribbon'
    assign lb_pct = settings.promo_second_pct | default: 30
    assign lb_campaign = settings.promo_label | default: 'تخفيضات الصيف'
    assign lb_short = settings.promo_badge_short | default: 'على الثانية'
    assign lb_long = settings.promo_badge_long | default: 'زيد قطعة ثانية وخد التخفيض'
  -%}

  {%- case lb_v -%}

    {%- when 'ribbon' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Sits inside .card-img (position:relative). Uses inset-inline-start so it
        mirrors to the right edge on the RTL storefront without a second rule.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="lb-promo-ribbon" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="lb-promo-ribbon__campaign">{{ lb_campaign }}</span>
        <span class="lb-promo-ribbon__rate" dir="ltr">&minus;{{ lb_pct }}%</span>
        <span class="lb-promo-ribbon__obj">{{ lb_short }}</span>
      </span>

    {%- when 'line' -%}
      <p class="lb-promo-line" dir="auto">
        <span class="lb-promo-line__rate" dir="ltr">&minus;{{ lb_pct }}%</span>
        <span class="lb-promo-line__obj">{{ lb_short }}</span>
      </p>

    {%- when 'pdp' -%}
      <div class="lb-promo-pdp" dir="auto">
        <p class="lb-promo-pdp__head">
          <span class="lb-promo-pdp__campaign">{{ lb_campaign }}</span>
          <span class="lb-promo-pdp__rate" dir="ltr">&minus;{{ lb_pct }}%</span>
          <span>{{ lb_short }}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="lb-promo-pdp__body">{{ lb_long }}</p>
        {%- comment -%}
          ⚠ WHICH ITEM SHOPIFY DISCOUNTS IS NOT ASSERTED HERE, ON PURPOSE.

          Shopify's BXGY engine picks the qualifying line itself, and the
          behaviour is not stated in the API reference. It is [Likely] the
          lowest-priced eligible item, but "likely" is not good enough for a
          sentence a customer reads before paying: if it resolves the other way,
          the page has quietly overstated the offer.

          So the default copy claims only what is true either way — it applies
          automatically, without a code, to one item per order (which IS
          guaranteed, by usesPerOrderLimit: 1 on the discount).

          BEFORE LAUNCH: put two eligible pieces of DIFFERENT prices in a real
          cart and read which line Shopify discounts. Once observed, this string
          may be tightened in the theme editor — it is a setting, not code.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="lb-promo-pdp__note">{{ settings.promo_note | default: 'كيبان أوتوماتيكيا فالسلة بلا كود · كيتطبق على قطعة وحدة فكل طلب.' }}</p>
      </div>

  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endif -%}
